{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1198918-what-spheres-would-a-robocop-type-character-need","id":1198918,"title":"What spheres would a Robocop type character need?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-23T18:19:01-07:00","id":1198918,"title":"What spheres would a Robocop type character need?","content":"<a href=\"http://robocop.wikia.com/wiki/RoboCop_(Peter_Weller\" target=\"_blank\">http://robocop.wikia.com/wiki/RoboCop_(Peter_Weller</a>) For reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T21:07:00-07:00","id":1198955,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Robocop himself wouldn't need to be Awakened. His actions in the movies could be replicated with a relatively small selection of Enhancements. Targeting software, recording devices, and a jack for plugging into external computers. A few minor things, like his ability to stow a pistol in his leg (which could be a custom Advantage). Some dots in Armor. Even his gun and jetpack (from Robocop 3) could just be Devices.<br /> <br /> When you get around to it, Robocop is basically a more overt HITMark. Or else a heavily modified Iteration X cyborg.<br /> <br /> Assuming he WERE Awakened, though, I'd probably give him Forces 3, Mind 1, Entropy 2, and maybe Life 1. Prime 2 would also be needed to use his jetpack, if it were an Instrument rather than a Device. Matter 1 might also be helpful, for the sake of analyzing materials, but we're being generous as to his capabilities, compared to the movies.<br /> <br /> I'd probably go with a starting character line-up of Forces 3, Prime 2, Entropy 1, or Entropy 2 if we were willing to shell out freebies for extra Sphere dots. If not, freebies (after the requisite 8 spent on Arete to 3) would be spent on Advantages (Armor and that weapon-stowing thing). Backgrounds would be dumped almost entirely into Enhancements and possibly Wonders, though Requisitions might also be in order. Might get more freebies by taking the Construct and Bizarre Hunger (baby food) flaws. If we're talking movie-version Robocop, he would also be sporting the Paranormal Prohibition flaw, reflecting Directive 4 (the inability to arrest or harm an OCP executive). As for Merits, things like Lightning Calculator, Code of Honor, Iron Will, and Insensate to Pain would all be good possibilities, though I'd first dump any extra freebie points into more Armor first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}